WEBVTT

1
00:00:51.865 --> 00:00:54.356
Hello. My friend Jacques Becker

2
00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:57.697
recreated a true story in all its detail.

3
00:00:58.038 --> 00:01:01.303
My story. It took place in 1947

4
00:01:02.509 --> 00:01:03.942
at the Santé prison

5
00:01:34.141 --> 00:01:35.165
Face front!

6
00:01:37.344 --> 00:01:38.140
Go ahead.

7
00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:45.617
Let him go in right away. I'm in a rush.

8
00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:47.118
Stand here!

9
00:01:51.024 --> 00:01:54.357
Maurice Gaillarbois, 32 yrs. Old.
Block 13, cell 35.

10
00:01:56.096 --> 00:01:59.156
The inmate has been refusing
to eat for 48 hours.

11
00:02:04.638 --> 00:02:06.333
Why are you on
a hunger strike?

12
00:02:06.406 --> 00:02:07.600
I'm innocent!

13
00:02:08.241 --> 00:02:12.940
You'll have a fair trial if you're innocent.
Meanwhile, eat.

14
00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.143
I don't want to eat, and I want
the judge to know I'm not eating

15
00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:19.578
because if I don't eat,
it's his fault!

16
00:02:19.753 --> 00:02:21.846
Okay, but the judge is eating.

17
00:02:22.556 --> 00:02:25.616
And knowing you don't eat
won't lessen his appetite.

18
00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:26.791
I won't eat!

19
00:02:28.728 --> 00:02:31.561
Okay, we'll tell him
you won't eat.

20
00:02:33.166 --> 00:02:33.894
Next!

21
00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:44.635
What's this?

22
00:02:46.213 --> 00:02:48.374
Gaspard, Claude, No. 6028.

23
00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:51.647
Hid a lighter, supposedly gold plated.

24
00:02:59.226 --> 00:03:02.627
You know very well
lighters are forbidden here.

25
00:03:03.563 --> 00:03:05.531
Even without fuel, sir?

26
00:03:05.699 --> 00:03:08.395
Even without fuel.
Strict regulations.

27
00:03:08.768 --> 00:03:11.828
Someone must have told you
when you first got here.

28
00:03:11.972 --> 00:03:15.066
Actually I forgot
it was in my pocket.

29
00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:18.742
- And then you found it.
- That's right

30
00:03:18.912 --> 00:03:21.278
Why didn't you give it
to a guard?

31
00:03:21.815 --> 00:03:23.908
It would be returned to you
upon your release.

32
00:03:23.984 --> 00:03:27.579
You're right, sir, but this
lighter has sentimental value.

33
00:03:27.754 --> 00:03:29.915
I like to look at it
now and again.

34
00:03:33.493 --> 00:03:35.893
- You say it's made of gold?
- Yes, sir.

35
00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.295
That's a valuable.
It will be returned to you.

36
00:03:41.368 --> 00:03:45.668
You deserve two weeks of mail-holding,
but I'll turn a blind eye this time.

37
00:03:45.739 --> 00:03:47.969
Thank you very much, sir.

38
00:03:53.013 --> 00:03:53.877
Nice guy!

39
00:03:55.282 --> 00:03:58.649
You'll get your lighter
when you get out.

40
00:04:27.113 --> 00:04:29.581
- Here's a new inmate!
- We're four already.

41
00:04:29.649 --> 00:04:32.277
- So now you're five.
- We're expecting work.

42
00:04:32.352 --> 00:04:35.014
We're getting cardboard to make boxes,
it'll take up a lot of room.

43
00:04:35.088 --> 00:04:38.114
No one's forcing you!
In custody, work is voluntary.

44
00:04:38.491 --> 00:04:40.482
- You don't like us working?
- Don't be a smart ass!

45
00:04:40.727 --> 00:04:42.456
We have a right to work
if we want to.

46
00:04:42.529 --> 00:04:44.588
I said, here's a new guy,
no arguments.

47
00:04:44.764 --> 00:04:46.857
I'll argue.
We're already four in here

48
00:04:46.933 --> 00:04:49.265
on top of the work we've
been waiting for.

49
00:04:49.336 --> 00:04:52.396
Put down your stuff here,
and you, shut up!

50
00:04:53.106 --> 00:04:55.631
- I'm being polite, sir!
- Let it go, Manu. That's the way it is.

51
00:04:55.742 --> 00:04:56.936
Damn straight!

52
00:04:59.412 --> 00:05:00.606
We'll bring you
a mattress later.

53
00:05:03.617 --> 00:05:05.346
Sorry, I didn't ask
to come here.

54
00:05:05.952 --> 00:05:06.919
Don't worry.

55
00:05:09.489 --> 00:05:13.289
My name's Vosselin, but you can call me
Monseigneur. It's my nickname.

56
00:05:13.426 --> 00:05:15.917
I'm Claude Gaspard.
I was in Block 8.

57
00:05:16.096 --> 00:05:19.554
- But they moved us due to repairs.
- You'll be okay here.

58
00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:23.034
- It doesn't feel that way.
- I said don't worry about that!

59
00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:26.066
Let's not start again.
What's done is done.

60
00:05:27.807 --> 00:05:29.206
- Roland Darbant.
- Hi!

61
00:05:31.611 --> 00:05:32.805
That's Geo Cassid.

62
00:05:37.484 --> 00:05:41.215
He's new. Moved from Block 8
on account of repairs.

63
00:05:41.788 --> 00:05:43.050
- Hi!
- Hello.

64
00:05:43.456 --> 00:05:44.616
Manu Borelli.

65
00:05:56.569 --> 00:05:59.129
You'll be okay here.
Bring your bag.

66
00:06:02.242 --> 00:06:04.233
Don't worry.
We'll put your stuff away.

67
00:06:05.478 --> 00:06:06.376
Put it on the bed.

68
00:06:07.547 --> 00:06:09.913
- Got a wardrobe at home?
- Yeah, why?

69
00:06:10.583 --> 00:06:13.313
Everyone has a wardrobe,
and a wife too.

70
00:06:14.354 --> 00:06:15.184
Got a wife?

71
00:06:16.489 --> 00:06:20.892
Don't answer him.
You don't have to talk about yourself.

72
00:06:22.228 --> 00:06:23.752
I don't mind talking about it.

73
00:06:25.165 --> 00:06:26.894
Things all right with your woman?

74
00:06:27.701 --> 00:06:29.396
No, I love someone else.

75
00:06:29.836 --> 00:06:32.737
- Was she a good lover, the other one?
- Geo, leave us alone, will you?

76
00:06:32.806 --> 00:06:36.503
Why? It's nice to talk about love,
it's healthy.

77
00:06:36.943 --> 00:06:38.968
You see,
Geo is interested in love.

78
00:06:39.212 --> 00:06:41.806
Women are interested in it too,
don't forget!

79
00:06:42.115 --> 00:06:44.583
He's a specialist.
Much in demand.

80
00:06:45.151 --> 00:06:48.177
Would you believe he had to hide
when he wanted to sleep alone!

81
00:06:51.424 --> 00:06:54.552
Hey guys. We brought you work.

82
00:06:56.396 --> 00:06:57.090
Let's go!

83
00:07:15.181 --> 00:07:16.944
What spirit!
That won't last long.

84
00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:18.847
We get bored in here!

85
00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.384
You're gonna make me bawl.

86
00:07:37.604 --> 00:07:40.095
- We brought you 5,000 sheets.
- We can count on you.

87
00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:43.573
- What luck, eh?
- Go ahead and laugh, I mean it.

88
00:07:43.743 --> 00:07:46.541
Sure, you won't even have time to eat.
Well, good luck!

89
00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:47.676
Good night.

90
00:07:52.986 --> 00:07:55.250
He's right,
this is a hell of a job!

91
00:07:55.789 --> 00:07:58.280
It'll be good for us.
You hear, Geo?

92
00:08:00.426 --> 00:08:01.393
Lazybones!

93
00:08:02.262 --> 00:08:03.786
He'll get to it.

94
00:08:03.863 --> 00:08:05.160
Come on, Manu!

95
00:08:17.177 --> 00:08:19.304
- Do you mind?
- Go ahead.

96
00:08:28.454 --> 00:08:30.888
Funny, I'm beginning
to like it.

97
00:08:34.093 --> 00:08:36.618
You all asked to work
or just you three?

98
00:08:36.696 --> 00:08:39.130
- All of us.
- You have to get to work.

99
00:08:40.099 --> 00:08:40.997
You promised, Geo.

100
00:08:41.434 --> 00:08:42.696
Wait, not yet.

101
00:08:43.837 --> 00:08:45.805
There's the soup trolley.

102
00:09:03.323 --> 00:09:05.917
- What's this?
- Chef's vermicelli special.

103
00:09:06.426 --> 00:09:08.587
You're all dirtbags in the kitchen!

104
00:09:08.661 --> 00:09:10.458
- You know, I...
- It's not his fault.

105
00:09:10.864 --> 00:09:12.263
I said they're dirtbags.

106
00:09:13.266 --> 00:09:14.358
Personal opinion, right?

107
00:09:42.629 --> 00:09:43.288
It's not edible.

108
00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:45.319
It looks foul.

109
00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.124
Disgusting.

110
00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:58.577
I won't insist.

111
00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:03.113
- Not all that bad.
- You're always hungry.

112
00:10:05.151 --> 00:10:07.585
Here, help yourselves!
There's enough for everyone.

113
00:10:08.187 --> 00:10:09.984
You're nice, but we
have all we need!

114
00:10:10.523 --> 00:10:12.889
Pack up your food;
you're our guest.

115
00:10:15.995 --> 00:10:17.860
Your little mistress
spoils you.

116
00:10:18.298 --> 00:10:20.163
Don't answer him
and sit down.

117
00:10:31.744 --> 00:10:32.438
That's good.

118
00:10:34.013 --> 00:10:34.945
It's disgusting.

119
00:10:40.019 --> 00:10:42.146
Here, eat. Help yourself.

120
00:10:43.923 --> 00:10:46.687
Goose liver!
You don't mess around.

121
00:10:46.993 --> 00:10:48.927
Yes, look honey,

122
00:10:49.662 --> 00:10:52.995
strawberry jam with real fruit,
chestnut spread.

123
00:10:53.366 --> 00:10:55.357
Manu likes chestnut spread!

124
00:10:56.569 --> 00:10:58.560
And I thought you all needed money.

125
00:10:58.838 --> 00:11:00.669
- Because of this stuff?
- Well, yes.

126
00:11:01.441 --> 00:11:03.671
Normally the only guys who work
are strapped for cash.

127
00:11:03.743 --> 00:11:05.301
There are those who are bored too.

128
00:11:05.445 --> 00:11:09.074
That's true, in cells where
they don't get along. Not here.

129
00:11:09.716 --> 00:11:12.344
You'll never get me to believe
this is why you wanted to work.

130
00:11:12.585 --> 00:11:14.382
So? What do you believe?

131
00:11:15.288 --> 00:11:18.746
I don't know.
I'm surprised you do, that's all.

132
00:11:19.292 --> 00:11:20.987
- Really?
- Yes, really.

133
00:11:21.494 --> 00:11:24.657
Tell us about your mistress.
That'll keep you from talking crap.

134
00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:28.792
May I have the spoon please?

135
00:11:33.306 --> 00:11:35.774
- You share everything?
- As you see.

136
00:11:36.175 --> 00:11:39.303
That's marvellous. I'm glad
I'm here with you guys.

137
00:11:39.645 --> 00:11:41.010
The pleasure is all ours.

138
00:11:42.582 --> 00:11:44.209
I can never tell whether
he's kidding or not.

139
00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.414
That's my charm.

140
00:11:46.853 --> 00:11:49.083
Have some, don't be shy.

141
00:11:49.889 --> 00:11:52.756
All right. If you'll share
whatever I get.

142
00:11:53.559 --> 00:11:55.083
You're a good man.
We're glad to have you.

143
00:12:09.909 --> 00:12:11.433
A little cigarette to top it off.

144
00:12:13.479 --> 00:12:13.968
Thanks.

145
00:12:27.326 --> 00:12:27.985
And Manu?

146
00:12:28.661 --> 00:12:29.628
Manu doesn't smoke.

147
00:12:32.398 --> 00:12:34.059
- Gaspard, Claude?
- That's me.

148
00:12:34.467 --> 00:12:36.628
There's a package for you
in your old block.

149
00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.000
Hold it.

150
00:12:45.611 --> 00:12:48.273
You look pleased,
all of a sudden. Why?

151
00:12:49.282 --> 00:12:50.476
I like the new guy.

152
00:12:53.653 --> 00:12:55.086
Yes, you can go.

153
00:12:55.755 --> 00:12:58.622
Manu, we have to decide.
Do we tell him or not?

154
00:12:58.791 --> 00:12:59.780
We tell him.

155
00:13:01.661 --> 00:13:03.253
You're in charge. You decide.

156
00:13:08.568 --> 00:13:10.058
Manu, we have to
tell the new guy.

157
00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:11.500
You too?

158
00:13:12.171 --> 00:13:14.036
Haven't got a choice.
We must start.

159
00:13:15.541 --> 00:13:17.168
You should wait.

160
00:13:18.377 --> 00:13:19.571
- Are you crazy?
- No.

161
00:13:19.946 --> 00:13:22.506
I don't trust strangers,
and what a stranger!

162
00:13:23.116 --> 00:13:25.641
- What do you know about him?
- You'll see.

163
00:13:26.285 --> 00:13:29.448
So you'll wait to be tried,
sentenced to death and beheaded?

164
00:13:29.689 --> 00:13:32.419
I have to deal with the courts, also.
Think of the others.

165
00:13:35.795 --> 00:13:38.355
I don't give a shit
about the new guy, but

166
00:13:38.931 --> 00:13:41.729
If it weren't him,
it'd be another.

167
00:13:42.835 --> 00:13:44.803
And he could be a drag.

168
00:15:00.713 --> 00:15:03.443
Gaspard, Claude,
Block 8 cell 26.

169
00:15:06.419 --> 00:15:07.977
What? You're in
Block 11 cell 6?

170
00:15:08.521 --> 00:15:10.853
Yes sir, I was in
Block 8 before.

171
00:15:11.023 --> 00:15:12.991
- How come?
- My cell was changed.

172
00:15:13.259 --> 00:15:14.021
I'll check that.

173
00:15:15.294 --> 00:15:18.229
Gaspard, Claude, Block 11 cell 6.
That's right.

174
00:16:13.586 --> 00:16:16.612
Smells good.
Looks like rice pudding...

175
00:16:17.256 --> 00:16:18.120
Must be, boss.

176
00:16:35.308 --> 00:16:36.240
Enjoy it! Next!

177
00:16:55.294 --> 00:16:58.695
- I see Geo's at it.
- You see well.

178
00:16:59.165 --> 00:17:01.133
I got some nice stuff.

179
00:17:02.168 --> 00:17:05.160
Chitterling sausage, smoked fish.

180
00:17:06.339 --> 00:17:08.000
Vanilla rice pudding.

181
00:17:08.274 --> 00:17:10.902
- From your sweetheart.
- Exactly.

182
00:17:11.811 --> 00:17:13.335
Who likes rice pudding?

183
00:17:15.514 --> 00:17:17.812
Me, but I'm not hungry now.

184
00:17:22.555 --> 00:17:25.456
- What's going on?
- Nothing, why?

185
00:17:25.825 --> 00:17:29.022
I don't know,
I have this feeling.

186
00:17:30.563 --> 00:17:32.963
While you were getting your package,
we talked about you.

187
00:17:33.866 --> 00:17:37.063
We're used to living here together,
the four of us

188
00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:40.803
and then you arrive,
so naturally we talk about you.

189
00:17:40.873 --> 00:17:45.139
Sorry, Manu wanted to say something.
I'd like to hear it.

190
00:17:45.211 --> 00:17:49.238
- We don't know you, nor you us.
- That's right.

191
00:17:49.782 --> 00:17:52.410
But we took you in right away.

192
00:17:52.551 --> 00:17:53.381
You're very kind.

193
00:17:54.086 --> 00:17:57.021
And without knowing it you've
landed in a cell that's a bit special.

194
00:17:58.791 --> 00:18:00.850
We're not all here
for the same reason.

195
00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:05.462
But in court, the luckiest
will get 10 years.

196
00:18:06.699 --> 00:18:09.133
As you see, my friends
and I risk a great deal.

197
00:18:09.301 --> 00:18:10.063
You do.

198
00:18:10.903 --> 00:18:14.339
So we'd like to know what
you're up against, Gaspard.

199
00:18:19.578 --> 00:18:22.479
I'm accused of attempted
first degree murder.

200
00:18:23.182 --> 00:18:24.911
That could get him 10 years easy.

201
00:18:25.084 --> 00:18:27.518
Do you mind...
Who's charging you?

202
00:18:28.053 --> 00:18:32.012
- My wife. One evening, at our Neuilly home.
- Congrats!

203
00:18:32.191 --> 00:18:34.523
Shut up, Monseigneur! Go on.

204
00:18:35.661 --> 00:18:38.027
I was with my wife
and her sister.

205
00:18:39.331 --> 00:18:40.389
We were arguing

206
00:18:42.201 --> 00:18:44.431
and my wife threatened me
with a shotgun.

207
00:18:45.638 --> 00:18:49.404
I wanted to take it from her
but it went off

208
00:18:49.575 --> 00:18:51.406
and she was wounded in the shoulder.

209
00:18:51.744 --> 00:18:55.544
Says you. But your wife must tell
a different story since you're here.

210
00:18:56.482 --> 00:18:59.610
My wife claims it was I who
drew the gun to shoot her.

211
00:19:00.719 --> 00:19:03.051
She was angry with you, eh!

212
00:19:03.789 --> 00:19:04.813
How old is your wife?

213
00:19:05.324 --> 00:19:07.315
Thirty. 3 years older than me.

214
00:19:07.793 --> 00:19:10.990
- And your sister-in-law?
- She's a kid. Seventeen.

215
00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:14.927
- Was she there?
- Yes. She backed my testimony.

216
00:19:16.068 --> 00:19:18.662
But hers was ruined
by a servant.

217
00:19:18.737 --> 00:19:19.601
Bitch!

218
00:19:20.139 --> 00:19:21.766
A woman who hates me.

219
00:19:22.541 --> 00:19:26.033
She told the judge
Nicole was upstairs with her.

220
00:19:26.779 --> 00:19:31.079
You say attempted first degree murder.
Why first degree?

221
00:19:32.885 --> 00:19:36.582
There were 3 shotguns in the
gun-rack, only 1 was loaded.

222
00:19:37.122 --> 00:19:38.817
What were you arguing about?

223
00:19:39.892 --> 00:19:41.985
Money. In principal, anyway.

224
00:19:42.561 --> 00:19:44.392
- Does Nicole screw well?
- What?

225
00:19:45.364 --> 00:19:47.161
See, he screws.

226
00:19:47.233 --> 00:19:48.427
Geo, that's enough!

227
00:19:49.368 --> 00:19:51.063
Were they regular lead
or buckshot?

228
00:19:52.071 --> 00:19:55.438
- Regular.
- Less fatal. Pity.

229
00:19:57.142 --> 00:19:59.372
- What happened to your wife?
- Nothing serious.

230
00:19:59.778 --> 00:20:01.006
Her left shoulder was hit.

231
00:20:02.214 --> 00:20:05.081
She's just having a bit
of a hard time right now.

232
00:20:05.718 --> 00:20:08.380
And she accuses you of wanting
to kill her. That's harsh!

233
00:20:09.722 --> 00:20:10.780
What can you do?

234
00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:12.818
You loaded the gun?

235
00:20:16.095 --> 00:20:17.119
Is your wife rich?

236
00:20:18.597 --> 00:20:19.655
Rich enough.

237
00:20:20.466 --> 00:20:25.199
What's your official income?
That's all that counts in court.

238
00:20:26.338 --> 00:20:27.430
I sold automobiles.

239
00:20:28.741 --> 00:20:30.174
In other words, you lived
off your wife's money.

240
00:20:31.544 --> 00:20:33.011
I guess.

241
00:20:33.946 --> 00:20:35.174
You'll get
20 years hard labor.

242
00:20:36.515 --> 00:20:37.982
- You think so?
- At least.

243
00:20:40.319 --> 00:20:40.876
Are you sure?

244
00:20:42.488 --> 00:20:46.185
Your case stinks. You wound
your wife who supports you.

245
00:20:46.725 --> 00:20:48.750
You sleep with her sister.
You sell used cars.

246
00:20:49.295 --> 00:20:50.660
The judges can't
stand that.

247
00:20:52.831 --> 00:20:54.355
20 years labor
is a long time.

248
00:20:55.734 --> 00:20:56.860
What's the matter with you?

249
00:20:58.437 --> 00:21:00.234
We wanted to know
what you're risking.

250
00:21:00.839 --> 00:21:04.138
Because we risk a great deal
waiting here quietly for appeal.

251
00:21:07.446 --> 00:21:08.276
What?

252
00:21:09.081 --> 00:21:10.173
We're going to escape.

253
00:21:12.885 --> 00:21:14.614
- From here?
- From here.

254
00:21:17.122 --> 00:21:18.384
You think we're crazy?

255
00:21:18.657 --> 00:21:19.715
No, not at all.

256
00:21:23.162 --> 00:21:27.428
Go on, Roland,
tell him all about it.

257
00:21:30.402 --> 00:21:32.063
He knows what he's doing.

258
00:21:32.871 --> 00:21:36.102
He's already escaped
three times; right Roland?

259
00:21:45.818 --> 00:21:48.981
When I think that if I hadn't changed cells
I wouldn't be going with you.

260
00:21:49.688 --> 00:21:50.518
I'm lucky!

261
00:21:51.323 --> 00:21:53.314
As long as you trust us, you're lucky.

262
00:21:59.331 --> 00:22:00.229
So when do we start?

263
00:22:00.666 --> 00:22:03.191
It's gonna be lights out soon.
We can't dig the hole at night.

264
00:22:03.268 --> 00:22:05.168
We have to take advantage
of the daily noises outside.

265
00:22:05.437 --> 00:22:06.495
Of course!

266
00:22:08.307 --> 00:22:10.775
Tonight we'll feast,
pass me that rice pudding.

267
00:22:11.477 --> 00:22:13.274
Give me the box, Roland.
We'll share everything.

268
00:22:13.479 --> 00:22:14.343
Dinner's served!

269
00:22:17.916 --> 00:22:20.180
Funny how you rub your
hands together. Suits you.

270
00:22:20.252 --> 00:22:22.846
Sure, I come from
a long line of clergymen.

271
00:22:23.122 --> 00:22:24.146
My uncle was a bishop.

272
00:22:25.524 --> 00:22:28.584
No kidding. I was wondering
about your name, Monseigneur.

273
00:22:29.795 --> 00:22:31.660
- Well, I'm going for it.
- Be my guest!

274
00:22:39.138 --> 00:22:40.469
Here we do nothing but eat.

275
00:23:34.626 --> 00:23:35.558
What's the matter?

276
00:23:37.763 --> 00:23:42.496
Nothing. I was thinking about
my grandmother. She raised me.

277
00:23:43.902 --> 00:23:44.926
Was she rich?

278
00:23:46.371 --> 00:23:48.896
Bloody Gaspard,
you were a happy kid.

279
00:23:51.143 --> 00:23:53.668
Yeah, I had everything
I wanted.

280
00:23:54.446 --> 00:23:56.607
You only mention your
grandmother. And your parents?

281
00:23:57.583 --> 00:24:00.450
My mom died at my birth, my dad
5 years later in a car accident.

282
00:24:02.121 --> 00:24:03.486
So you had no one
but your grandmother.

283
00:24:06.558 --> 00:24:09.721
I also had paternal grandparents
who couldn't afford to keep me.

284
00:24:10.763 --> 00:24:12.128
She's still alive,
your grandmother?

285
00:24:12.998 --> 00:24:15.091
No, why?

286
00:24:16.034 --> 00:24:18.298
So you're her heir.
You're rich?

287
00:24:21.507 --> 00:24:22.531
I was, yes.

288
00:24:24.076 --> 00:24:27.978
Pissed it all away. Then you met
a woman full of dough. Right?

289
00:24:28.714 --> 00:24:30.944
My wife has money,
but that had nothing to do with it.

290
00:24:31.016 --> 00:24:33.985
Don't be mad,
I'd have done the same thing.

291
00:24:34.620 --> 00:24:37.714
Only if I'd married a rich woman
I wouldn't have shot her.

292
00:24:38.190 --> 00:24:39.384
That's where you went wrong

293
00:24:40.559 --> 00:24:42.459
You're starting to get
on our nerves, Monseigneur!

294
00:24:42.661 --> 00:24:43.958
Never mind, no harm done.

295
00:24:44.129 --> 00:24:46.029
You're getting on my nerves too
with your crap.

296
00:24:46.098 --> 00:24:48.931
I want to sleep,
so shut up everybody. Got it?

297
00:24:52.471 --> 00:24:53.460
Okay.

298
00:25:30.475 --> 00:25:31.339
Emile!

299
00:25:33.679 --> 00:25:35.579
Here, Mercier, you can finish up.

300
00:26:12.351 --> 00:26:13.215
Slept well?

301
00:26:14.987 --> 00:26:16.215
Feels weird to be here.

302
00:26:16.388 --> 00:26:18.481
That always happens
when you change cells.

303
00:26:19.524 --> 00:26:22.288
I was thinking about it all.
Didn't get much sleep.

304
00:26:22.361 --> 00:26:26.388
Don't worry. Look,
they're sound asleep.

305
00:26:32.437 --> 00:26:33.768
- Good morning.
- Good morning, Roland.

306
00:26:40.012 --> 00:26:41.138
No one needs the doctor?

307
00:26:41.380 --> 00:26:42.278
I don't think so.

308
00:26:48.153 --> 00:26:48.949
Rise and shine!

309
00:27:06.104 --> 00:27:07.799
Give us sugar and the cookies.

310
00:27:10.542 --> 00:27:11.907
There.

311
00:27:20.786 --> 00:27:24.313
Luckily, there's sugar.
Their coffee tastes like hell.

312
00:28:28.720 --> 00:28:29.516
This one's nice.

313
00:28:30.722 --> 00:28:33.213
Get all the glass slivers
so we don't cut ourselves.

314
00:28:33.725 --> 00:28:34.692
One thing at a time.

315
00:28:54.513 --> 00:28:56.413
- Who's the oldest here?
- Me.

316
00:28:56.782 --> 00:28:58.374
Stay here. The others out.

317
00:29:01.153 --> 00:29:01.983
Handkerchief.

318
00:29:06.725 --> 00:29:07.487
All right.

319
00:29:08.293 --> 00:29:09.157
That's all?

320
00:29:13.065 --> 00:29:13.690
Next.

321
00:29:20.238 --> 00:29:21.000
Your turn.

322
00:29:23.608 --> 00:29:25.473
- Give me that.
- Hurry up!

323
00:29:29.314 --> 00:29:29.905
All right.

324
00:29:42.094 --> 00:29:42.890
Who pulled the chain?

325
00:29:43.228 --> 00:29:45.253
I did. I'd never done it
from out here.

326
00:29:45.330 --> 00:29:46.558
Quit horsing around.

327
00:29:51.303 --> 00:29:54.636
Okay, move over.

328
00:29:58.110 --> 00:29:58.940
Move.

329
00:30:47.125 --> 00:30:47.750
Let's go!

330
00:30:52.397 --> 00:30:53.227
You can get back in!

331
00:31:01.706 --> 00:31:03.867
- They didn't spare us.
- Now everything's a mess.

332
00:31:04.309 --> 00:31:06.277
On the contrary,
it's good for us.

333
00:31:06.578 --> 00:31:09.445
- How's that?
- They won't be back too soon.

334
00:31:10.115 --> 00:31:12.583
Put the stuff away,
I've got work to do.

335
00:31:53.024 --> 00:31:55.959
You see, this little thing
acts as a periscope.

336
00:32:18.617 --> 00:32:21.643
It's perfect. You see
the hall in both directions.

337
00:32:25.156 --> 00:32:28.592
We've already had a search,
so we're okay on that front.

338
00:32:28.760 --> 00:32:30.057
We can start digging today.

339
00:32:33.665 --> 00:32:34.597
It's coming from No. 8.

340
00:32:44.442 --> 00:32:47.036
- I'm listening.
- Package for No. 4. Ready?

341
00:32:47.312 --> 00:32:48.108
Wait!

342
00:32:51.316 --> 00:32:55.878
Tell them we're waiting for masons and
we can't send anything until further notice.

343
00:32:57.989 --> 00:32:58.887
Swing!

344
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:09.898
Ready, No. 4?

345
00:33:18.243 --> 00:33:18.971
Send it over.

346
00:33:29.921 --> 00:33:33.652
Listen, no more packages today.
We're waiting for the masons.

347
00:33:35.327 --> 00:33:37.852
- Did you hear that, No. 8?
- All right, thank you.

348
00:33:45.303 --> 00:33:46.235
That way we'll have
some peace.

349
00:33:46.871 --> 00:33:48.896
Let's go.
Who's the lookout?

350
00:33:49.140 --> 00:33:49.868
Me, if you want.

351
00:33:55.814 --> 00:33:59.011
Okay. But stay sharp,
tell us everything you see.

352
00:33:59.551 --> 00:34:00.449
You can count on me.

353
00:34:06.858 --> 00:34:08.849
Go on working, I don't
need you right now.

354
00:34:18.703 --> 00:34:20.136
- Someone's coming.
- What?

355
00:34:20.905 --> 00:34:23.271
- Some guys with blankets.
- Screw it. It's not for us.

356
00:34:44.929 --> 00:34:45.520
Let me see.

357
00:34:48.233 --> 00:34:50.030
It's heavy; you wouldn't think it.

358
00:34:52.270 --> 00:34:53.134
It will do.

359
00:34:55.407 --> 00:34:56.374
Geo, come on!

360
00:36:05.076 --> 00:36:05.804
Move!

361
00:36:13.618 --> 00:36:15.711
It'll take too much time.
You have to hit harder!

362
00:36:15.954 --> 00:36:17.546
I think you're right.
No other way.

363
00:36:18.289 --> 00:36:20.814
In one hour either we break
through or get caught.

364
00:36:29.901 --> 00:36:30.959
You're crazy, it's impossible!

365
00:36:31.903 --> 00:36:33.962
If anything saves us,
it'll be the noise.

366
00:37:00.265 --> 00:37:00.924
They're here.

367
00:37:21.352 --> 00:37:22.080
They moved along.

368
00:38:44.936 --> 00:38:45.630
Your turn, Geo.

369
00:42:01.532 --> 00:42:04.296
Monseigneur, it's no use
looking out, you know.

370
00:42:04.769 --> 00:42:05.599
Are you crazy? Why?

371
00:42:06.304 --> 00:42:08.033
If they come now
we'd be fried anyway.

372
00:42:08.639 --> 00:42:09.537
What's wrong with you?

373
00:42:25.256 --> 00:42:27.486
Can't see a thing.
Give me some cardboard.

374
00:42:44.008 --> 00:42:44.997
We're there.

375
00:42:50.381 --> 00:42:51.177
We go down tonight.

376
00:42:51.782 --> 00:42:52.510
May I?

377
00:42:57.154 --> 00:43:00.146
Now you've seen, move it,
we have to throw it all in.

378
00:44:27.878 --> 00:44:28.640
Let's try.

379
00:44:33.985 --> 00:44:34.644
Well?

380
00:44:36.454 --> 00:44:37.250
Not bad.

381
00:44:44.061 --> 00:44:46.291
Try to pull the string more lightly.

382
00:44:46.764 --> 00:44:49.665
I'd like to, but you see,
it works one way and not the other.

383
00:44:49.734 --> 00:44:51.224
Don't pull so hard.

384
00:44:51.402 --> 00:44:53.302
Roland, closing time.

385
00:45:15.059 --> 00:45:19.155
Gentlemen, closing time.
Clean up before you go to sleep.

386
00:45:19.530 --> 00:45:20.326
All right.

387
00:45:26.737 --> 00:45:28.728
We have 15 minutes
before the first round.

388
00:46:19.090 --> 00:46:19.886
He's coming.

389
00:46:22.893 --> 00:46:24.087
Get in bed quick.

390
00:47:00.097 --> 00:47:00.927
Let's go!

391
00:47:01.665 --> 00:47:02.757
He was early, damn it!

392
00:48:09.600 --> 00:48:11.568
- Alright?
- Okay. Come down.

393
00:48:13.037 --> 00:48:17.997
Monseigneur, take the string
and rock.

394
00:48:44.401 --> 00:48:44.992
Okay?

395
00:48:51.942 --> 00:48:53.671
That's an underground chamber
like this one.

396
00:48:59.984 --> 00:49:01.645
That's the large cellar.

397
00:49:01.819 --> 00:49:03.514
Why is it lit?

398
00:49:04.588 --> 00:49:05.452
Listen.

399
00:49:10.995 --> 00:49:11.927
It's deserted.

400
00:49:12.429 --> 00:49:14.989
At night, except for the
patrol, no one comes here.

401
00:49:15.332 --> 00:49:17.596
I'll cut this bar,
that'll do.

402
00:49:21.405 --> 00:49:23.202
What if guards come by
and hear us?

403
00:49:23.807 --> 00:49:26.241
I'll file 20 times,
and stop to listen.

404
00:49:26.877 --> 00:49:28.003
And so on.

405
00:50:41.218 --> 00:50:42.116
Finish it!

406
00:51:20.557 --> 00:51:21.182
Let's go.

407
00:51:41.044 --> 00:51:42.375
That's a corridor.

408
00:51:48.819 --> 00:51:50.013
There's so much stuff down here.

409
00:51:50.554 --> 00:51:53.045
This is where they store
their material.

410
00:52:34.198 --> 00:52:35.631
The patrol must come down here

411
00:52:41.038 --> 00:52:42.938
Another corridor.

412
00:52:47.478 --> 00:52:49.571
They punch in.

413
00:52:59.490 --> 00:53:03.085
See that one? I'll cut here

414
00:53:03.794 --> 00:53:06.024
and make a master key.

415
00:53:23.046 --> 00:53:24.638
Her husband sold
rabbit furs.

416
00:53:26.817 --> 00:53:28.148
Another trade that's
disappeared.

417
00:53:32.556 --> 00:53:33.648
She was beautiful.

418
00:53:36.126 --> 00:53:37.093
There.

419
00:53:53.076 --> 00:53:58.104
One day the guy caught us.
What a mess!

420
00:53:58.649 --> 00:53:59.445
Really!

421
00:53:59.750 --> 00:54:02.810
I thought we'd fight it out
but nothing happened.

422
00:54:02.886 --> 00:54:05.116
He turned around
and left us there.

423
00:54:05.188 --> 00:54:06.780
- And then?
- Well... then.

424
00:54:06.957 --> 00:54:10.393
I saw the chick 2-3 times
and then got posted to Paris.

425
00:54:10.561 --> 00:54:12.153
So obviously I stopped
seeing her.

426
00:55:26.670 --> 00:55:28.729
They left through there.
We'll do the same.

427
00:56:11.615 --> 00:56:13.048
Where are we going?

428
00:56:13.517 --> 00:56:14.449
Look.

429
00:56:16.987 --> 00:56:19.387
This is the rough map
of the prison basement.

430
00:56:23.126 --> 00:56:26.095
We came from here.
At every corner of the prison

431
00:56:26.263 --> 00:56:28.493
there's a similar room,
all interconnected.

432
00:56:28.665 --> 00:56:31.327
By corridors like this one.

433
00:56:31.501 --> 00:56:34.436
I see. But where is
the sewer shaft?

434
00:56:35.005 --> 00:56:36.370
Maybe in one of the halls.

435
00:56:37.607 --> 00:56:38.767
Maybe in the corridors.

436
00:56:45.682 --> 00:56:47.047
Maybe there are several.

437
00:57:13.443 --> 00:57:15.502
They have only
one type of lock.

438
00:57:15.645 --> 00:57:20.014
Yes, like the cell doors.
So guards don't need 100 keys.

439
00:58:45.635 --> 00:58:49.503
Give me some more light.
There!

440
00:58:50.173 --> 00:58:52.164
Look at this animal.

441
00:58:52.576 --> 00:58:55.238
Here comes your snack, baby!

442
00:59:04.855 --> 00:59:06.117
Look!

443
00:59:14.297 --> 00:59:16.231
See you soon.

444
00:59:43.360 --> 00:59:45.260
What the hell were
they talking about?

445
00:59:45.328 --> 00:59:47.660
I didn't understand
a word they said.

446
01:00:24.100 --> 01:00:25.124
Look.

447
01:00:28.138 --> 01:00:30.197
That's the door to the well.

448
01:00:30.974 --> 01:00:34.375
Only this is a
damn spring lock.

449
01:00:47.958 --> 01:00:50.153
- What are you doing?
- I'll file the hinges

450
01:00:50.660 --> 01:00:53.060
- The door won't hold.
- Let me do it!

451
01:00:53.129 --> 01:00:54.562
They check it, look.

452
01:00:54.864 --> 01:00:55.990
They won't notice.

453
01:01:48.885 --> 01:01:49.852
Fantastic!

454
01:02:00.063 --> 01:02:00.791
Give me a hinge.

455
01:02:25.789 --> 01:02:26.551
Give me the other one.

456
01:02:44.107 --> 01:02:44.732
And now?

457
01:02:45.442 --> 01:02:46.272
You'll see.

458
01:03:01.724 --> 01:03:02.281
<i>All right?</i>

459
01:03:02.826 --> 01:03:03.554
All right.

460
01:03:16.873 --> 01:03:18.966
This way, we'll know if they
came through while we were below.

461
01:03:28.218 --> 01:03:28.877
Your turn.

462
01:03:47.604 --> 01:03:48.229
It works.

463
01:04:18.334 --> 01:04:21.462
This is concrete. No use trying.
Let's check the other one.

464
01:04:35.785 --> 01:04:37.446
Think they come
down here often?

465
01:04:37.520 --> 01:04:40.011
Just the sewage workers,
and probably not often.

466
01:04:53.670 --> 01:04:56.104
- They've got us trapped.
- Is it that hard?

467
01:04:56.172 --> 01:04:57.332
See for yourself.

468
01:05:14.657 --> 01:05:17.455
That's not concrete,
it's cheap cement. It'll give.

469
01:05:17.961 --> 01:05:19.019
What do you mean?

470
01:05:19.762 --> 01:05:21.957
This is right in the curve.

471
01:05:22.298 --> 01:05:24.596
We'll dig a tunnel
around the plug.

472
01:05:24.667 --> 01:05:27.329
- That'll take weeks.
- It's a matter of days.

473
01:05:27.437 --> 01:05:29.598
We'll come back tomorrow with tools.

474
01:06:08.544 --> 01:06:09.670
They came by.

475
01:06:09.846 --> 01:06:11.473
Put the door back in place.

476
01:06:27.530 --> 01:06:28.497
We didn't come this way.

477
01:06:28.831 --> 01:06:31.664
It's shorter this way.
We've almost come full circle.

478
01:07:31.828 --> 01:07:33.261
Tomorrow, this'll be our crowbar.

479
01:07:59.622 --> 01:08:00.987
Just 5 more cells.

480
01:08:05.294 --> 01:08:05.988
It won't work.

481
01:08:07.797 --> 01:08:09.230
They already removed
the boards.

482
01:08:11.934 --> 01:08:12.958
Hurry up, they're coming!

483
01:08:14.670 --> 01:08:15.466
<i>Coming!</i>

484
01:08:17.373 --> 01:08:18.271
Hurry up!

485
01:08:25.214 --> 01:08:25.976
Come on, Roland!

486
01:08:32.555 --> 01:08:33.487
Hurry!

487
01:08:34.123 --> 01:08:35.055
Quick, the dummies!

488
01:09:05.121 --> 01:09:06.110
Hello there!

489
01:09:08.691 --> 01:09:09.453
Hello, sir!

490
01:09:12.061 --> 01:09:14.029
They're all asleep
in there!

491
01:09:14.430 --> 01:09:16.022
Gotta dream, sir!

492
01:09:16.632 --> 01:09:17.997
You sleep fully dressed
these days?

493
01:09:19.802 --> 01:09:21.827
I've always been
sensitive to the cold.

494
01:09:28.511 --> 01:09:29.603
What happened to you?

495
01:09:31.147 --> 01:09:32.910
You're already dressed.
How come?

496
01:09:33.549 --> 01:09:36.450
Funny guy. We were getting ready
to go to the hole.

497
01:09:36.519 --> 01:09:39.283
- Nothing like trust.
- Tell us what happened.

498
01:09:39.355 --> 01:09:42.449
- We found a way out. Right?
- I believe so.

499
01:09:42.525 --> 01:09:43.992
Why didn't you
come up earlier?

500
01:09:44.060 --> 01:09:46.756
Do you have a watch? No!
Well, neither do we.

501
01:09:48.464 --> 01:09:50.159
That can't go on.

502
01:10:01.677 --> 01:10:04.737
Now let's try not to make
life difficult, shall we?

503
01:10:08.684 --> 01:10:11.676
Life! You could say
she came at me full on.

504
01:10:11.854 --> 01:10:15.654
The clap and the slammer at once.
That's a lot for one man, I tell you.

505
01:10:15.725 --> 01:10:19.525
No women ever, kid!
That's the secret.

506
01:10:19.595 --> 01:10:21.563
Well, to each his own.
Right doc?

507
01:10:24.333 --> 01:10:25.664
No men either!

508
01:10:26.102 --> 01:10:29.469
That's a good one!
So you manage alone?

509
01:10:29.572 --> 01:10:31.699
Listen, you want
your face punched?

510
01:10:32.508 --> 01:10:36.308
Forget it.
Let's see your nose!

511
01:10:43.853 --> 01:10:45.047
Just a drop.

512
01:10:52.094 --> 01:10:52.856
Thanks.

513
01:10:53.396 --> 01:10:54.829
Whenever you want.
At your service.

514
01:11:28.230 --> 01:11:29.094
Sir, please.

515
01:11:55.191 --> 01:11:56.055
Arms up.

516
01:11:58.594 --> 01:11:59.686
Stop playing games.

517
01:12:05.601 --> 01:12:06.533
Why did you take sand?

518
01:12:06.869 --> 01:12:09.235
To scour our bowls.
What's so wrong?

519
01:12:10.006 --> 01:12:12.372
Gotta keep things clean
and since we have nothing...

520
01:12:19.682 --> 01:12:20.307
Thanks, sir!

521
01:12:48.878 --> 01:12:52.041
Exactly 30 minutes. Every half hour
we flip it upside-down, make a mark,

522
01:12:52.348 --> 01:12:55.181
this way we can tell the time
and be safe.

523
01:12:55.618 --> 01:12:56.585
Super!

524
01:14:21.470 --> 01:14:22.664
The block is about three feet wide.

525
01:14:24.607 --> 01:14:27.633
We'll have to dig a 10-foot tunnel.
Let's set up the boards.

526
01:14:31.447 --> 01:14:32.414
Let's have them.

527
01:14:40.189 --> 01:14:43.488
With this we're sure not
to block the grooves with debris.

528
01:15:12.421 --> 01:15:13.183
Give me that one.

529
01:16:53.555 --> 01:16:54.522
Let me see.

530
01:17:00.396 --> 01:17:02.387
Say, you made a real key!

531
01:17:02.464 --> 01:17:06.264
With this, the others can move
around the cellar without me.

532
01:17:52.614 --> 01:17:56.106
Manu, it's 2 a.m.
Gotta get back.

533
01:18:31.120 --> 01:18:32.052
The guards.

534
01:19:10.893 --> 01:19:11.985
They just came by.

535
01:19:13.562 --> 01:19:15.393
Hurry down. Roland's
waiting for you below.

536
01:19:35.050 --> 01:19:37.780
What filth!
It's not easy, I tell you.

537
01:19:43.292 --> 01:19:43.917
See you.

538
01:19:55.537 --> 01:19:56.902
It's over there.

539
01:19:58.874 --> 01:20:00.000
It's over there, Geo.

540
01:20:15.257 --> 01:20:18.283
I just spent 28 minutes
to get you and come back.

541
01:20:23.132 --> 01:20:25.930
- It's hard, I warn you.
- We do our best.

542
01:20:26.335 --> 01:20:28.599
Good luck.
I better get some sleep.

543
01:20:32.708 --> 01:20:35.176
Don't forget the time.
Remember the hourglass.

544
01:20:35.244 --> 01:20:37.041
Go get some sleep.

545
01:20:40.582 --> 01:20:41.412
He's incredible.

546
01:20:42.417 --> 01:20:44.681
Yeah. Okay, I'll start.

547
01:21:11.079 --> 01:21:14.014
- Manu, it's amazing.
- What?

548
01:21:15.384 --> 01:21:16.510
I never experienced this.

549
01:21:17.920 --> 01:21:18.648
What?

550
01:21:20.088 --> 01:21:21.715
You might think it's strange

551
01:21:22.124 --> 01:21:24.991
but it's the first time in
my life that I feel right.

552
01:21:27.162 --> 01:21:28.823
I swear to you it's true.

553
01:21:29.965 --> 01:21:32.263
It's great to be
with guys like you.

554
01:21:36.104 --> 01:21:39.164
Yeah, I think I've changed.

555
01:21:40.475 --> 01:21:42.705
I think it's because
of you and Roland.

556
01:22:06.235 --> 01:22:08.760
What do they think down there?

557
01:22:09.071 --> 01:22:12.302
It'll work, they'll manage
with the key as well as I do.

558
01:22:12.374 --> 01:22:15.468
Say, Geo handles
the shaft door very well.

559
01:22:15.544 --> 01:22:17.478
He managed
to replace it in one go.

560
01:22:17.546 --> 01:22:19.343
I'd never have thought him capable.

561
01:22:22.918 --> 01:22:24.010
Everything's okay in the hall.

562
01:22:26.121 --> 01:22:26.985
I'm going to lie down.

563
01:22:39.701 --> 01:22:43.364
He should go down too.
I'll take him tomorrow night.

564
01:22:45.040 --> 01:22:45.972
Okay.

565
01:22:46.141 --> 01:22:48.336
Get some sleep, you need it.

566
01:23:18.407 --> 01:23:19.305
Thanks, Manu.

567
01:23:44.966 --> 01:23:47.059
The faucet's leaking
more and more.

568
01:23:48.403 --> 01:23:51.839
The joint's rotten.
It can burst at any time.

569
01:23:51.907 --> 01:23:55.104
If that happens at night,
we'll have visitors.

570
01:23:57.212 --> 01:24:00.010
Gotta take care of it right away.
Monseigneur, go knock.

571
01:24:09.691 --> 01:24:11.488
It's a nuisance having
the plumbers here.

572
01:24:12.427 --> 01:24:13.325
We have no choice.

573
01:24:14.229 --> 01:24:15.491
You don't like workers,
do you?

574
01:24:15.797 --> 01:24:19.164
Sleep, Geo, sleep!
Ah, this guy!

575
01:24:21.870 --> 01:24:23.132
- Hello, sir!
- Well?

576
01:24:23.405 --> 01:24:24.929
Our faucet's leaking.
Waste of water.

577
01:24:25.374 --> 01:24:29.401
Great, they busted the faucet;
now I have to look for a plumber.

578
01:24:30.145 --> 01:24:31.908
This one isn't dead, I hope?

579
01:24:31.980 --> 01:24:33.572
We like you too much
to give you trouble.

580
01:24:33.982 --> 01:24:36.951
If we wanted to die we'd wait
till you were off duty.

581
01:24:37.018 --> 01:24:40.886
These guys are capable of suicide,
of anything really!

582
01:24:40.956 --> 01:24:43.424
- Capable of the best too.
- Very well put.

583
01:24:43.492 --> 01:24:46.290
You'd have made a good lawyer.
Okay, I'll send the plumbers in.

584
01:24:46.428 --> 01:24:49.363
Meanwhile, get ready for your walk.
It's just about time.

585
01:24:59.207 --> 01:24:59.639
Hello, sir!

586
01:24:59.808 --> 01:25:00.604
Hello!

587
01:25:04.946 --> 01:25:06.413
Hello, guys.

588
01:25:09.418 --> 01:25:11.579
Try to fix this, and hurry!

589
01:25:18.560 --> 01:25:20.721
- So it's leaking?
- See for yourself!

590
01:25:20.862 --> 01:25:23.854
It's running day and night
and gets on our nerves.

591
01:25:25.133 --> 01:25:28.534
Time for exercise!

592
01:25:29.738 --> 01:25:32.229
Stupid jerk.
He's always in a hurry!

593
01:25:35.844 --> 01:25:37.675
Time for your walk,
let's move it!

594
01:25:40.582 --> 01:25:42.516
Behave yourselves on the way.

595
01:25:52.527 --> 01:25:53.289
Exercise time.

596
01:25:55.897 --> 01:25:56.625
Let's move.

597
01:26:09.578 --> 01:26:10.943
Exercise time.
Let's move.

598
01:26:14.916 --> 01:26:16.042
Behave yourselves on the way.

599
01:26:27.429 --> 01:26:28.123
Exercise time.

600
01:26:31.500 --> 01:26:32.899
Let's get moving.

601
01:27:01.496 --> 01:27:04.226
See, it stopped leaking.
Try not to break it again.

602
01:27:04.299 --> 01:27:05.266
Thanks, sir.

603
01:27:09.938 --> 01:27:11.428
Now we'll have some quiet.

604
01:27:12.307 --> 01:27:14.138
They were surprisingly fast.

605
01:27:14.442 --> 01:27:16.706
They didn't even wait
for their reward.

606
01:27:16.778 --> 01:27:20.077
Yeah, that's strange.
Usually these guys beg.

607
01:27:24.753 --> 01:27:26.983
That's it, they stole
my cigarettes.

608
01:27:28.657 --> 01:27:30.682
Mine too, a whole new
pack of Gauloises.

609
01:27:34.596 --> 01:27:37.224
They swiped my stamps,
two whole sets.

610
01:27:38.667 --> 01:27:40.498
That's it, nothing more?

611
01:27:40.569 --> 01:27:43.265
- No food missing.
- Nor here.

612
01:27:43.505 --> 01:27:46.099
Lucky me, I don't think
they touched my stuff.

613
01:27:50.712 --> 01:27:51.576
What're you doing?

614
01:27:52.013 --> 01:27:53.571
Let it go!
It's not worth the trouble.

615
01:27:54.149 --> 01:27:55.047
I think it is.

616
01:27:58.420 --> 01:27:59.444
What now?

617
01:27:59.888 --> 01:28:02.118
Sir, is M. Grinval here?

618
01:28:02.190 --> 01:28:03.623
Yeah, I just ran into him. Why?

619
01:28:03.692 --> 01:28:06.388
Do me a favor and ask him to stop by.

620
01:28:10.532 --> 01:28:11.294
All right.

621
01:28:16.838 --> 01:28:17.702
Who's Grinval?

622
01:28:18.173 --> 01:28:19.197
Block Chief.

623
01:28:23.612 --> 01:28:27.241
Hello, M. Grinval. Excuse us,
but here's what happened.

624
01:28:27.315 --> 01:28:29.283
The plumbers were here
while we were out in the yard.

625
01:28:29.584 --> 01:28:31.916
- And?
- They're smoking our cigarettes.

626
01:28:32.220 --> 01:28:34.211
And mailing their letters home
with our stamps.

627
01:28:34.789 --> 01:28:36.256
What were they doing here?

628
01:28:36.591 --> 01:28:37.751
Our faucet was leaking.

629
01:28:51.506 --> 01:28:56.068
This faucet's too tight now.
I'll be back with the plumbers.

630
01:28:56.444 --> 01:28:57.411
Thank you, M. Grinval.

631
01:29:05.553 --> 01:29:07.350
Now we'll get our exercise.

632
01:29:10.392 --> 01:29:11.324
You asked for us, M. Grinval.

633
01:29:16.331 --> 01:29:17.298
Come in.

634
01:29:22.537 --> 01:29:23.561
Take a look at the faucet.

635
01:29:23.872 --> 01:29:25.931
We just fixed it, M. Grinval.

636
01:29:26.307 --> 01:29:26.966
See you!

637
01:29:32.647 --> 01:29:33.909
Here buddy, have a smoke!

638
01:29:37.886 --> 01:29:38.875
What do you want from us?

639
01:29:49.497 --> 01:29:50.964
That's enough, Geo,
you're being vicious.

640
01:29:53.401 --> 01:29:54.129
Search him.

641
01:30:08.416 --> 01:30:09.246
Hand over the goods.

642
01:30:14.189 --> 01:30:14.985
Assholes!

643
01:30:19.627 --> 01:30:21.720
Next time, ask.
It'll be cheaper.

644
01:30:25.667 --> 01:30:28.135
- Job done?
- Yes, M. Grinval. Thanks.

645
01:30:34.442 --> 01:30:36.103
You may join the work team
in Block 3.

646
01:30:36.377 --> 01:30:37.139
Yes, sir.

647
01:30:38.246 --> 01:30:39.110
Let's go!

648
01:30:44.085 --> 01:30:44.949
Everything all right?

649
01:30:45.286 --> 01:30:46.378
Perfect, sir. Thank you.

650
01:30:50.658 --> 01:30:51.522
Well, well...

651
01:30:52.494 --> 01:30:53.461
I liked that.

652
01:30:56.164 --> 01:30:57.188
Here are your smokes.

653
01:30:57.365 --> 01:30:59.765
You really told 'em.
You were fantastic!

654
01:31:01.302 --> 01:31:03.167
You got good paws, Geo.

655
01:31:13.948 --> 01:31:14.972
You're not serious, Manu.

656
01:31:17.752 --> 01:31:19.982
With all that's going on.
You're acting like a kid.

657
01:31:20.221 --> 01:31:21.210
Whatever!

658
01:33:03.157 --> 01:33:06.524
Roland, I'm not
leaving with you.

659
01:33:07.128 --> 01:33:07.787
What?

660
01:33:08.763 --> 01:33:09.593
I'm staying here.

661
01:33:11.866 --> 01:33:12.924
You don't trust us any more?

662
01:33:13.968 --> 01:33:18.462
On the contrary, I'm sure
you'll make it, that's why.

663
01:33:21.342 --> 01:33:24.311
I don't know if I told you

664
01:33:25.346 --> 01:33:27.974
but when I was arrested
my mother almost dropped dead.

665
01:33:40.228 --> 01:33:44.187
If I escape, the police
will go to her again.

666
01:33:46.100 --> 01:33:48.933
That could kill her,
so I'm staying.

667
01:33:54.509 --> 01:33:55.908
I'm not telling
the others yet.

668
01:34:36.451 --> 01:34:37.418
Let me have a drink.

669
01:34:48.997 --> 01:34:50.464
It's going well,
we're not far any more.

670
01:34:55.837 --> 01:34:57.361
Too bad you're not
coming with us.

671
01:34:59.073 --> 01:34:59.903
I'm going to work.

672
01:35:41.149 --> 01:35:42.116
You're okay?

673
01:35:44.118 --> 01:35:46.484
We must be getting close,
it's getting hard again.

674
01:36:09.544 --> 01:36:10.238
Geo!

675
01:36:13.181 --> 01:36:14.375
Answer me! Geo!

676
01:37:12.340 --> 01:37:13.364
There, he's awake.

677
01:37:14.775 --> 01:37:15.605
Did you sleep well?

678
01:37:17.745 --> 01:37:19.906
You're real dirty!
You must have really hit hard.

679
01:37:20.715 --> 01:37:22.910
Sure did. Didn't we, Geo?

680
01:37:34.362 --> 01:37:34.919
Next!

681
01:37:51.212 --> 01:37:54.079
Hello, who? Gaspard, Claude?

682
01:37:55.449 --> 01:37:56.677
He's right here.
I'll send him over.

683
01:37:58.853 --> 01:37:59.842
Visiting room.

684
01:38:02.456 --> 01:38:03.184
Lucky you!

685
01:38:03.658 --> 01:38:04.454
Kiss her for me.

686
01:38:17.038 --> 01:38:17.868
Gaspard, Claude.

687
01:38:19.607 --> 01:38:20.266
No. 1.

688
01:38:25.479 --> 01:38:28.505
- How'd you do it?
- Through the lawyer's secretary.

689
01:38:28.950 --> 01:38:33.546
I manage. Not like you.
You can't even send a letter.

690
01:38:35.323 --> 01:38:36.722
If I could only write you.

691
01:38:39.694 --> 01:38:42.561
Tell me, you're still
staying at your sister's?

692
01:38:42.930 --> 01:38:45.990
The house is just as much as mine
as it is hers. But we don't talk.

693
01:38:46.534 --> 01:38:50.595
We eat in separate rooms.
She's still madly in love with you.

694
01:38:50.805 --> 01:38:52.500
I hear her sobbing in bed at night.

695
01:38:55.343 --> 01:38:57.504
If you would see her,
she'd come right away.

696
01:38:57.878 --> 01:38:59.038
What makes you say that?

697
01:38:59.580 --> 01:39:02.174
If you'd ask her yourself,
she'd withdraw charges.

698
01:39:02.917 --> 01:39:05.078
That's not what the lawyer
told me last time.

699
01:39:05.620 --> 01:39:07.178
He said she flatly refused.

700
01:39:08.422 --> 01:39:09.548
She wants to punish us.

701
01:39:11.158 --> 01:39:14.355
Listen, I've been thinking.
I'll go to England for a year.

702
01:39:14.895 --> 01:39:15.987
It'll calm her down.

703
01:39:17.298 --> 01:39:18.060
Why England?

704
01:39:18.899 --> 01:39:21.060
To study English.
I always wanted to.

705
01:39:23.504 --> 01:39:25.699
Nicole, if you knew how
much I want.

706
01:39:26.707 --> 01:39:27.639
I want.

707
01:39:30.878 --> 01:39:34.177
When you get out I'll come back.
Then we could...

708
01:39:36.150 --> 01:39:37.447
And you, don't you want it?

709
01:39:38.886 --> 01:39:40.114
You're so curious!

710
01:39:43.658 --> 01:39:45.717
Don't play games, Nicole.
It annoys me.

711
01:40:12.853 --> 01:40:15.788
You! Where are you going?

712
01:40:16.724 --> 01:40:19.818
I'm going...
Sorry, Chief.

713
01:40:20.394 --> 01:40:22.589
I made a mistake.
This is my old cell.

714
01:40:23.164 --> 01:40:25.257
Let me see your pass.

715
01:40:32.440 --> 01:40:34.908
You're from Block 11, right?
The other way.

716
01:40:35.710 --> 01:40:37.234
I'd really like to put you in the hole.

717
01:40:37.678 --> 01:40:39.908
- Let me explain, sir.
- What would you explain?

718
01:40:40.548 --> 01:40:43.073
- Going to make a deal?
- I assure you it was a mistake.

719
01:40:43.584 --> 01:40:44.744
What's going on?

720
01:40:44.952 --> 01:40:48.388
Here's an inmate of Block 11
on his way back from a visit.

721
01:40:48.556 --> 01:40:50.353
Instead of going back to his
own cell he came here.

722
01:40:56.330 --> 01:40:59.925
I'm sorry, sir,
I was just going to explain.

723
01:41:01.702 --> 01:41:03.795
I do belong to Block 11,
cell 6

724
01:41:05.306 --> 01:41:08.036
but before that I was
in Block 8, cell 26.

725
01:41:09.443 --> 01:41:12.571
You want the warden to believe
you suddenly lost your memory.

726
01:41:13.347 --> 01:41:15.076
I'm sorry, that's exactly
what happened.

727
01:41:16.117 --> 01:41:19.052
I was coming back from a visit,
and totally confused.

728
01:41:20.054 --> 01:41:21.419
These things happen, don't they?

729
01:41:22.123 --> 01:41:23.590
I know you, I think.

730
01:41:24.225 --> 01:41:27.661
Yes, sir. I bothered you
about a trifle.

731
01:41:28.329 --> 01:41:30.627
I kept a cigarette lighter,
a golden one

732
01:41:31.599 --> 01:41:33.499
Oh, yes. What's your name?

733
01:41:34.668 --> 01:41:35.896
Claude Gaspard, sir.

734
01:41:37.738 --> 01:41:39.296
Yes. Go back to your cell

735
01:41:40.307 --> 01:41:41.934
and in the future,
try to be more attentive.

736
01:41:42.943 --> 01:41:45.309
Absolutely, sir. Thank you.

737
01:42:12.807 --> 01:42:14.399
- Want some?
- No thank you, later.

738
01:42:21.615 --> 01:42:22.479
Our friend isn't talkative.

739
01:42:23.484 --> 01:42:24.508
Nor are you.

740
01:42:25.419 --> 01:42:27.114
We haven't had a visit.

741
01:42:29.256 --> 01:42:31.156
So you want the story.

742
01:42:32.460 --> 01:42:35.793
No, just tell us if she's
a blond or a brunette.

743
01:42:36.764 --> 01:42:37.628
Come on.

744
01:42:40.601 --> 01:42:43.331
Yes, I just saw a woman.
That's what you wanted to know.

745
01:42:44.338 --> 01:42:48.035
May I ask one question?
Just answer yes or no.

746
01:42:48.676 --> 01:42:50.166
Ask away, I don't promise
anything.

747
01:42:51.345 --> 01:42:53.813
After making love, does she
pick your blackheads?

748
01:42:59.687 --> 01:43:01.211
Does she or doesn't she?

749
01:43:02.056 --> 01:43:02.750
Shit.

750
01:43:38.792 --> 01:43:41.727
- What a pleasant visit.
- Isn't it?

751
01:43:42.263 --> 01:43:44.959
- You don't trust us, do you?
- I do, I do.

752
01:43:45.232 --> 01:43:49.134
We know you're model inmates,
but we have our duties.

753
01:43:49.370 --> 01:43:51.736
Good, because we
appreciate you.

754
01:43:51.872 --> 01:43:53.169
- Really!
- Don't we?

755
01:43:53.307 --> 01:43:54.331
Absolutely.

756
01:43:55.442 --> 01:43:59.003
Anyway, I don't see why you came
suddenly like this.

757
01:43:59.079 --> 01:44:02.105
We didn't mean to.
We've seen Freddy across the hall.

758
01:44:02.182 --> 01:44:03.877
What did he do?

759
01:44:04.018 --> 01:44:06.418
We're looking for a file
hidden in a desk blotter.

760
01:44:07.454 --> 01:44:08.216
So?

761
01:44:08.789 --> 01:44:10.154
I see you haven't got any

762
01:44:10.824 --> 01:44:13.816
but you've got cardboard.
You could make one.

763
01:44:17.598 --> 01:44:19.793
All we make here are boxes.
No desk blotter.

764
01:44:20.301 --> 01:44:22.633
So did you find it?

765
01:44:23.704 --> 01:44:26.434
Curious, aren't you?
Want to know everything.

766
01:44:27.441 --> 01:44:30.410
You'll meet Freddy one day
and he'll tell you.

767
01:44:30.811 --> 01:44:32.904
He must have been worried
when he saw you.

768
01:44:33.080 --> 01:44:35.048
One always gets worried
when they see me.

769
01:44:40.387 --> 01:44:42.252
You're kind to clean up.

770
01:44:49.396 --> 01:44:50.522
Don't stand there, move!

771
01:45:03.978 --> 01:45:04.808
<i>Pierre!</i>

772
01:45:12.720 --> 01:45:13.550
Come on, we're off.

773
01:45:17.725 --> 01:45:18.384
See you!

774
01:45:24.131 --> 01:45:25.428
I thought we were done for.

775
01:45:26.900 --> 01:45:27.730
Terrible!

776
01:45:29.670 --> 01:45:31.638
We have to dig,
get through and piss off.

777
01:45:38.679 --> 01:45:41.011
Tonight or tomorrow.
Otherwise we're screwed.

778
01:47:20.981 --> 01:47:21.572
Gaspard!

779
01:47:23.951 --> 01:47:24.781
What is it?

780
01:47:25.219 --> 01:47:26.379
This is it, look.

781
01:47:27.921 --> 01:47:28.819
We're on the other side.

782
01:48:23.911 --> 01:48:24.536
My jacket.

783
01:48:38.792 --> 01:48:39.486
Let's go!

784
01:49:13.760 --> 01:49:14.454
There's an exit.

785
01:49:19.266 --> 01:49:19.925
Come.

786
01:49:32.646 --> 01:49:33.237
Come have a look.

787
01:49:37.784 --> 01:49:38.910
Look at the prison.

788
01:49:46.660 --> 01:49:47.354
Imagine!

789
01:49:57.070 --> 01:49:57.832
A cab!

790
01:50:15.355 --> 01:50:16.720
We could almost take it.

791
01:50:19.126 --> 01:50:19.922
Listen!

792
01:50:23.931 --> 01:50:28.834
6 o'clock.
Let's go get the others.

793
01:51:14.047 --> 01:51:14.809
That's it, Roland!

794
01:51:16.650 --> 01:51:17.947
- What?
- You won.

795
01:51:19.019 --> 01:51:22.682
We got through, we were in
the main sewer, then in the streets.

796
01:51:23.423 --> 01:51:24.151
The street?

797
01:51:25.325 --> 01:51:28.158
Yes. Gaspard even wanted
to take a cab.

798
01:51:30.564 --> 01:51:32.498
Tonight we'll be out of here.

799
01:51:55.255 --> 01:51:56.085
Just a second.

800
01:52:00.560 --> 01:52:02.152
- The youngest picks.
- Why me?

801
01:52:02.496 --> 01:52:03.986
Because you're
the youngest. Pick.

802
01:52:08.035 --> 01:52:09.969
- Monseigneur.
- Bravo, Monseigneur!

803
01:52:11.338 --> 01:52:12.828
Good, the eldest will
lead the way.

804
01:52:14.074 --> 01:52:15.632
Go ahead, pick another!

805
01:52:21.415 --> 01:52:22.040
Go on!

806
01:52:27.320 --> 01:52:28.287
Go on!

807
01:52:30.857 --> 01:52:33.792
Roland. And Gaspard.

808
01:52:35.062 --> 01:52:38.862
You go last, kid,
but if you want my turn, it's okay.

809
01:52:39.166 --> 01:52:41.726
- He'll take mine.
- Why? No reason for that.

810
01:52:41.802 --> 01:52:45.067
- There is. I'm not going.
- What?

811
01:52:45.839 --> 01:52:48.103
I'm not going.
Roland knows.

812
01:52:48.875 --> 01:52:49.739
Since when?

813
01:52:50.277 --> 01:52:55.408
Since I told him. I did work.
Did my share, okay?

814
01:53:00.887 --> 01:53:06.154
We can't say anything.
You're old enough to do as you choose.

815
01:53:11.064 --> 01:53:12.429
Yeah, I'm old enough.

816
01:53:19.005 --> 01:53:21.838
Gaspard goes second
instead of Geo.

817
01:53:27.414 --> 01:53:30.178
Hello! Are you Gaspard, Claude?

818
01:53:31.418 --> 01:53:32.715
- Yes, why?
- Come with me.

819
01:53:32.986 --> 01:53:34.248
- Where to?
- You'll see.

820
01:53:36.857 --> 01:53:38.791
Take your jacket and
button your collar.

821
01:53:41.628 --> 01:53:43.858
M. Grinval, where are you
taking him like that?

822
01:53:43.930 --> 01:53:45.659
You're too curious, Borelli!

823
01:53:49.503 --> 01:53:51.437
- Are you ready?
- Any time.

824
01:53:59.546 --> 01:54:00.410
What does this mean?

825
01:54:03.583 --> 01:54:06.177
It means that the director
just summoned him.

826
01:54:08.688 --> 01:54:09.712
What's the occasion?

827
01:54:10.924 --> 01:54:11.788
I don't know!

828
01:54:21.301 --> 01:54:21.960
This way.

829
01:54:34.948 --> 01:54:36.108
Gaspard, warden.

830
01:54:39.920 --> 01:54:40.887
Thank you, Grinval.

831
01:54:42.422 --> 01:54:43.150
Have a seat.

832
01:54:47.527 --> 01:54:51.122
- Feeling good since yesterday?
- Very well, thank you.

833
01:54:51.198 --> 01:54:53.666
You don't have a good sense
of direction, do you?

834
01:54:53.767 --> 01:54:56.634
If it weren't for me, you'd have
ended up in the hole for a week.

835
01:54:56.770 --> 01:55:00.228
- My apologies again, sir.
- You're very educated and nice.

836
01:55:00.974 --> 01:55:03.772
- That helps in life.
- I haven't noticed.

837
01:55:04.077 --> 01:55:07.410
I'll prove it to you.
I looked into your case

838
01:55:07.781 --> 01:55:10.443
and found out something that
will interest you enormously.

839
01:55:11.318 --> 01:55:12.342
What is it, sir?

840
01:55:13.887 --> 01:55:15.980
- In a minute.
- Sorry.

841
01:55:16.590 --> 01:55:20.993
Here is the charge against you.

842
01:55:22.429 --> 01:55:26.092
Attempted first degree murder.

843
01:55:28.034 --> 01:55:31.435
Actually I'm accused of wounding
my wife with a gunshot.

844
01:55:31.504 --> 01:55:34.530
How did that happen?
Look, I'm not interrogating you.

845
01:55:34.608 --> 01:55:39.136
That's not my line of duty.
This is a private conversation.

846
01:55:39.312 --> 01:55:42.611
I know, sir,
and I appreciate it.

847
01:55:44.017 --> 01:55:46.383
With your permission,
I'll tell you all about it.

848
01:55:47.988 --> 01:55:49.080
Go ahead!

849
01:55:51.191 --> 01:55:54.024
In two words, we had a fight,
my wife and I.

850
01:55:54.594 --> 01:55:57.654
She threatened me with a shotgun.
I wanted to take it from her

851
01:55:57.831 --> 01:55:59.731
but it went off
and she was wounded.

852
01:56:01.735 --> 01:56:05.398
I wish it had been me.
Anyway, she recovered fast.

853
01:56:05.739 --> 01:56:08.264
- As fast as that?
- She's in perfect shape.

854
01:56:09.442 --> 01:56:11.410
So why didn't she
withdraw charges?

855
01:56:12.512 --> 01:56:16.642
Because Committing Magistrate
M. Labourdette told her not to.

856
01:56:17.217 --> 01:56:19.412
You see I'm not everyone's
cup of tea, sir.

857
01:56:20.420 --> 01:56:24.220
- You think it's the magistrate?
- My attorney certainly does.

858
01:56:24.758 --> 01:56:28.091
You believe a magistrate can
pressure a witness like that.

859
01:56:28.461 --> 01:56:31.294
Especially a woman,
jealous and in love.

860
01:56:31.931 --> 01:56:34.092
How do you know my
wife is in love?

861
01:56:34.234 --> 01:56:36.600
Because she withdrew her
charges yesterday.

862
01:56:39.306 --> 01:56:41.866
- So I'm going to be released.
- Probably.

863
01:56:42.742 --> 01:56:45.302
As soon as the magistrate
dismisses the case.

864
01:56:46.346 --> 01:56:48.246
Maybe not tomorrow,
but soon.

865
01:56:54.187 --> 01:56:55.552
You don't seem very pleased.

866
01:57:00.827 --> 01:57:04.058
What are you thinking about?
Tell me.

867
01:57:05.899 --> 01:57:07.196
Perhaps I can help.

868
01:57:17.977 --> 01:57:19.103
I'm coming, sir.

869
01:57:56.483 --> 01:57:59.884
All right, back to your cell.

870
01:58:01.087 --> 01:58:01.883
Yes, M. Grinval.

871
01:58:34.087 --> 01:58:35.679
What are you waiting for?
Arms up!

872
01:58:52.071 --> 01:58:56.007
Something incredible happened.
My wife withdrew her charges.

873
01:58:59.646 --> 01:59:01.341
It is beyond me.

874
01:59:05.185 --> 01:59:06.083
Can you imagine?

875
01:59:07.220 --> 01:59:08.881
How do you know?

876
01:59:09.222 --> 01:59:10.553
The warden just told me.

877
01:59:17.363 --> 01:59:18.955
What do you think of that?

878
01:59:29.676 --> 01:59:33.112
- So you're not coming with us?
- Of course I am.

879
01:59:33.847 --> 01:59:35.439
- Are you crazy?
- Listen.

880
01:59:35.849 --> 01:59:38.249
I know my story better
than you, no?

881
01:59:38.518 --> 01:59:41.919
My wife backed off but I'm
still in for at least 5 years.

882
01:59:48.027 --> 01:59:50.757
- What makes you think that?
- You told me yourself

883
01:59:50.930 --> 01:59:54.263
that the court won't
like my story one bit.

884
01:59:57.770 --> 02:00:01.206
For me not to go to court,
the magistrate has to dismiss the case.

885
02:00:01.574 --> 02:00:04.168
Magistrate Labourdette
certainly won't do that.

886
02:00:05.879 --> 02:00:08.006
The warden told you all this?

887
02:00:10.083 --> 02:00:12.950
No. I know it just as
well as he does.

888
02:00:14.587 --> 02:00:17.055
What the hell were you doing
in his office for 2 hours?

889
02:00:18.658 --> 02:00:21.718
He's a nice guy. He's interested
in my case. That's all.

890
02:00:23.029 --> 02:00:26.965
Right. That's why
he kept you for 2 hours.

891
02:00:28.501 --> 02:00:29.695
He always does that!

892
02:00:32.038 --> 02:00:34.768
Every day he summons an
inmate just to chat.

893
02:00:36.976 --> 02:00:38.000
Did you have tea?

894
02:00:40.713 --> 02:00:41.737
What are you saying?

895
02:00:48.521 --> 02:00:51.684
Tell us what happened.
You went to see the warden.

896
02:00:52.125 --> 02:00:55.356
He told you the good news
and then what? Tell us.

897
02:00:57.964 --> 02:00:58.988
What's the matter with you?

898
02:00:59.799 --> 02:01:00.925
Tell us what you told him.

899
02:01:08.274 --> 02:01:11.937
Manu, you're crazy.
You think I betrayed you?

900
02:01:14.447 --> 02:01:15.471
Is that it?

901
02:01:23.089 --> 02:01:24.420
I believed you were my friend.

902
02:02:07.433 --> 02:02:08.365
I'm sorry.

903
02:02:12.772 --> 02:02:13.500
It's okay.

904
02:03:23.843 --> 02:03:25.003
Guys, he's here.

905
02:03:39.092 --> 02:03:39.854
Go!

906
02:03:53.873 --> 02:03:55.101
They're already asleep?

907
02:03:56.075 --> 02:03:59.272
That's right. I'm the only one
who works around here.

908
02:04:00.179 --> 02:04:01.441
You're one to talk.

909
02:04:01.814 --> 02:04:02.542
I swear!

910
02:04:19.265 --> 02:04:20.027
All clear.

911
02:04:27.440 --> 02:04:28.429
What a tie!

912
02:04:28.841 --> 02:04:31.503
A piece of blanket
will always be a piece of blanket.

913
02:04:31.844 --> 02:04:32.538
Go!

914
02:04:55.635 --> 02:04:56.465
Bye, Geo.

915
02:04:58.237 --> 02:04:59.226
Come on, Roland.

916
02:05:26.132 --> 02:05:26.996
Manu.

917
02:06:17.516 --> 02:06:18.642
God, don't!

918
02:06:23.990 --> 02:06:25.981
Let go of me,
it's no use!

919
02:06:29.295 --> 02:06:31.320
Undress them. Hurry.

920
02:06:45.077 --> 02:06:46.601
Are you okay?
Do you need help?

921
02:06:47.213 --> 02:06:48.202
Thank you, I'll manage.

922
02:06:53.386 --> 02:06:55.047
It's all over.
They go into solitary confinement.

923
02:07:05.498 --> 02:07:08.695
We're done here. Come out
the other way. It'll be easier.

924
02:08:15.034 --> 02:08:15.966
Cell No. 7.

925
02:08:37.623 --> 02:08:38.521
Poor Gaspard.

926
02:09:40.486 --> 02:09:44.752
You have been watching

927
02:09:44.924 --> 02:09:48.690
a film by Jacques Becker.

928
02:09:48.861 --> 02:09:53.628
THE HOLE
